  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Gender Equality in Solomon Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment&apos;s overall goal is to contribute to greater gender equality and social inclusion in the Solomon Islands. 
The objective is to support gender equality and social inclusion in the Solomon Islands. There are three end of program outcomes (EOPOs): 
EOPO1: LEADERSHIP - Australian assistance to targeted CSOs contributes to improved women&#x2019;s leadership and increased participation in national and provincial elections by 2027. 
EOPO2: ECONOMIC EMPOWERMENT&#x2013; Women have increased advocacy skills and business training and enabling greater participation in their businesses and local markets (including market vendors) by 2027. EOPO3: MAINSTREAMING &#x2013; Women&#x2019;s Development Division, in the Solomon Islands Government implement policies and programs that deliver improved gender equality.
The program will be delivered by trusted partners including IWDA, UN Women and local organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
